
  <sn><md>### Healthy Life, Better Living

![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/Food%20and%20Nutirition%20Thumbnail.png)

:::.p-2
**flow**
necessary-for ▪️ affect ▪️ energy-conversion ▪️ digestion ▪️ assimilation 
:::

- We cannot live without food. Several types of food are regularly necessary for the growth and development of the body, repair and replacement of worn-out tissues, and for producing energy etc. 
- Our health depends largely on the quality of the food we take. Food can `affect` in our `appearance, work, behaviour and standard of life`. 
-  During the `process of respiration` the `chemical energy of food is converted into thermal energy` and other forms of energy. Every living being takes food from the environment according to its need. 
- Each type of food is a complex chemical compound. This `complex food is broken down into simpler substance` by different types of ++enzymes++ in different parts of our digestive system. This process is called **digestion**. 
- The `digested food is then absorbed into the protoplasm` of body cells. This is called ++assimilation++.
After digestion the indigestible part of the food excreted from of the body through a special process.
