<sn><md>#### Food and Nutrition

According to the nutrition science, `all that we eat is not food`. The edible items that help produce energy, support growth, repair and immunity- in short, nourish the body- are called food. Nutrition is- getting necessary food items from the environment and digesting and absorbing them, then fulfilling the energy need, developing the immunity of diseases, and supporting the growth of the body. On the other hand, the organic and inorganic elements in food which provide the energy required for living body are collectively called the nutrients e.g. glucose, minerals and vitamins etc. The `three main functions` of food are-

1. growth and development, repair and protection of the body.
2. production of heat and energy.
3. protecting the body from diseases and keeping the body healthy, energetic and active.</md></sn>